[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-ARI-004
VERSION: 1
TITLE: Division
STATEMENT: >>>
When the service receives a valid division request with a divisor other than
zero, the service **shall** return the quotient `a ÷ b`, exact if it has at
most **20** fractional digits, otherwise rounded to **20** fractional digits
with ties rounded away from zero.
<<<
KIND: functional
STATUS: draft
PRIORITY: high
SAFETY: QM
RELEASE: 1.0.0
VERIFICATION: test
VERIF_LEVELS: unit, system
TAGS: arithmetic, division, rounding
SOURCE: Stakeholder request, 2026-11-18
OWNER: msforenter090
CREATED: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
RATIONALE: >>>
Unlike the other operations, a quotient can have infinitely many fractional
digits (1 ÷ 3), so a limit and a rounding rule are needed. Rounding ties
away from zero is the rule most people learn at school.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
- The limit of 20 fractional digits and the rounding rule are *proposed*
  and must be confirmed by the stakeholder.
- The rounded quotient is then written in canonical form, so trailing
  zeros are removed (`10 ÷ 4` gives `2.5`, not `2.50000000000000000000`).
- Division by zero is handled by REQ-VAL-002.
<<<
